.TH "DOCUMENT.CREATEATTRIBUTE" "3JS" "April 6, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
Document.createAttribute \- Document: createAttribute() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
The \f[B]\f[CB]createAttribute()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]Document\f[R] interface creates a new attribute node.
.PP
The object created is a node implementing the \f[CR]Attr\f[R] interface.
The DOM does not enforce what sort of attributes can be added to a
particular element in this manner.
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] The string given in parameter is converted to lowercase.
.RE
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
createAttribute(localName)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]localName\f[R]
A string containing the name of the attribute.
The value is used to initialize the new attribute\(cqs
\f[CR]localName\f[R] property.
.SS Return value
An \f[CR]Attr\f[R] node.
.SS Exceptions
.TP
\f[B]InvalidCharacterError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
Thrown if the \f[CR]localName\f[R] value is not a valid attribute name.
It must have at least one character, and may not contain ASCII
whitespace, \f[CR]NULL\f[R], \f[CR]/\f[R], \f[CR]=\f[R] or \f[CR]>\f[R]
(U+0000, U+002F, U+003D, or U+003E, respectively).
.RS
.RS
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] Earlier versions of the specification were more
restrictive, requiring that the \f[CR]localName\f[R] be a valid \c
.UR https://www.w3.org/TR/xml/#dt-name
XML name
.UE \c
\&.
.RE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Basic example
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] node = document.getElementById(\(dqdiv1\(dq);
\f[B]const\f[R] a = document.createAttribute(\(dqmy_attrib\(dq);
a.value = \(dqnewVal\(dq;
node.setAttributeNode(a);
console.log(node.getAttribute(\(dqmy_attrib\(dq)); \f[I]// \(dqnewVal\(dq\f[R]
.EE
